<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Datu Pagbuaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Datu Pagbuaya was a 16th-century chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohol">Bohol</a> coast in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. According to Spanish accounts, after raiders from Ternate attacked Bohol around 1563 he led many survivors to the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a>, where they founded Dapitan. He and his people later allied with the Spanish expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi">Miguel López de Legazpi</a>.</p></div>
